# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LICENSING-CRITICAL. Do not remove or narrow these patterns.
#
# The charter's most important rule is "never commit Paizo content" (CLAUDE.md,
# Rules data; docs/adr/0003-rules-data-licensing.md). Upstream packs are
# downloaded at setup time and converted output is written here. None of it may
# ever enter git history, which is permanent.
#
# A CI job independently fails the build if anything under these paths becomes
# tracked, because .gitignore alone cannot stop `git add -f`.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# Downloaded upstream foundryvtt/pf2e packs (pinned commit + checksum)
systems/pf2e/.data/upstream/

# Our converted, Zod-validated output
systems/pf2e/.data/imported/

# User world folders: world.db, assets/, snapshots/
worlds/

# SQLite databases anywhere
*.db
*.db-wal
*.db-shm
